Package: enetLTS
Type: Package
Title: Robust and Sparse Methods for High Dimensional Linear, Binary and
        Multinomial Regression
Version: 1.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Fatma Sevinc", "Kurnaz", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "fatmasevinckurnaz@gmail.com"),
    person("Irene", "Hoffmann", role = "aut"),
    person("Peter", "Filzmoser", role = "aut"))
Description: Fully robust versions of the elastic net estimator for linear,
        binary and multinomial regression, in particular for high dimensional
        data. The algorithm searches for outlier-free subsets on which the
        classical elastic net estimator can be applied. A reweighting step is
        added to improve the statistical efficiency of the estimators. The
        tuning parameters of the elastic net penalty are selected by
        cross-validation. The methods are described in Kurnaz, Hoffmann and
        Filzmoser (2018) <doi:10.1016/j.chemolab.2017.11.017> and in Kurnaz and
        Filzmoser (2023) <doi:10.1007/s10618-023-00936-6>.
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0), glmnet, parallel, stats, robustbase, robustHD,
        grDevices
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/fatmasevinck/enetLTS
BugReports: https://github.com/fatmasevinck/enetLTS/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
LazyData: true
NeedsCompilation: no
